Table full name: bigquery-public-data.san_francisco.sffd_service_calls
Column name: call_number Type: INT64 Description: A unique 9-digit number assigned by the 911 Dispatch Center (DEM) to this call. These number are used for both Police and Fire calls.
Column name: unit_id Type: STRING Description: Unit Identifier. For example E01 for Engine 1 or T01 for Truck 1.
Column name: incident_number Type: INT64 Description: A unique 8-digit number assigned by DEM to this Fire incident.
Column name: call_type Type: STRING Description: Type of call the incident falls into. See the list below.
Column name: call_date Type: DATE Description: Date the call is received at the 911 Dispatch Center. Used for reporting purposes.
Column name: watch_date Type: DATE Description: Watch date when the call is received. Watch date starts at 0800 each morning and ends at 0800 the next day.
Column name: received_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Date and time of call is received at the 911 Dispatch Center.
Column name: entry_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Date and time the 911 operator submits the entry of the initical call information into the CAD system
Column name: dispatch_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Date and time the 911 operator dispatches this unit to the call.
Column name: response_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Date and time this unit acknowledges the dispatch and records that the unit is en route to the location of the call.
Column name: on_scene_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Date and time the unit records arriving to the location of the incident
Column name: transport_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: If this unit is an ambulance, date and time the unit begins the transport unit arrives to hospital
Column name: hospital_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: If this unit is an ambulance, date and time the unit arrives to the hospital.
Column name: call_final_disposition Type: STRING Description: Disposition of the call (Code). For example TH2: Transport to Hospital - Code 2, FIR: Resolved by Fire Department
Column name: available_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Date and time this unit is not longer assigned to this call and it is available for another dispatch.
Column name: address Type: STRING Description: Address of midblock point associated with incident (obfuscated address to protect caller privacy)
Column name: city Type: STRING Description: City of incident
Column name: zipcode_of_incident Type: STRING Description: Zipcode of incident
Column name: battalion Type: STRING Description: Emergency Response District (There are 9 Fire Emergency Response Districts)
Column name: station_area Type: STRING Description: Fire Station First Response Area associated with the address of the incident
Column name: box Type: STRING Description: Fire box associated with the address of the incident. A box is the smallest area used to divide the City. Each box is associated with a unique unit dispatch order. The City is divided into more than 2,400 boxes.
Column name: original_priority Type: STRING Description: Initial call priority (Code 2: Non-Emergency or Code 3:Emergency).
Column name: priority Type: STRING Description: Call priority (Code 2: Non-Emergency or Code 3:Emergency).
Column name: final_priority Type: INT64 Description: Final call priority (Code 2: Non-Emergency or Code 3:Emergency).
Column name: als_unit Type: BOOL Description: Does this unit includes ALS (Advance Life Support) resources? Is there a paramedic in this unit?
Column name: call_type_group Type: STRING Description: Call types are divided into four main groups: Fire, Alarm, Potential Life Threatening and Non Life Threatening.
Column name: number_of_alarms Type: INT64 Description: Number of alarms associated with the incident. This is a number between 1 and 5.
Column name: unit_type Type: STRING Description: Unit type
Column name: unit_sequence_in_call_dispatch Type: INT64 Description: A number that indicates the order this unit was assigned to this call
Column name: fire_prevention_district Type: STRING Description: Bureau of Fire Prevention District associated with this address
Column name: supervisor_district Type: STRING Description: Supervisor District associated with this address
Column name: neighborhood_district Type: STRING Description: Neighborhood District associated with this address, boundaries available here: https://data.sfgov.org/d/p5b7-5n3h
Column name: location Type: STRING Description: Latitude and longitude of address obfuscated either to the midblock, intersection or call box
Column name: row_id Type: STRING Description: Unique identifier used for managing data updates. It is the concatenation of Call Number and Unit ID separated by a dash
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude of the address
Column name: longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude of the address
Sample rows:
[{'call_number': 122570160, 'unit_id': 'KM10', 'incident_number': 12084932, 'call_type': 'Medical Incident', 'call_date': '2012-09-13', 'watch_date': '2012-09-13', 'received_timestamp': '2012-09-13 12:44:55+00:00', 'entry_timestamp': '2012-09-13 12:46:22+00:00', 'dispatch_timestamp': '2012-09-13 12:46:33+00:00', 'response_timestamp': '2012-09-13 12:47:18+00:00', 'on_scene_timestamp': '2012-09-13 13:01:09+00:00', 'transport_timestamp': '2012-09-13 13:16:59+00:00', 'hospital_timestamp': '2012-09-13 13:37:24+00:00', 'call_final_disposition': 'Patient Declined Transport', 'available_timestamp': '2012-09-13 13:37:44+00:00', 'address': '600 Block of MERCHANT ST', 'city': 'SF', 'zipcode_of_incident': '94111', 'battalion': 'B01', 'station_area': '13', 'box': '0124', 'original_priority': '1', 'priority': '1', 'final_priority': 2, 'als_unit': False, 'call_type_group': 'Non Life-threatening', 'number_of_alarms': 1, 'unit_type': 'PRIVATE', 'unit_sequence_in_call_dispatch': 1, 'fire_prevention_district': '1', 'supervisor_district': '3', 'neighborhood_district': '', 'location': '(37.7949086758744, -122.404037735679)', 'row_id': '122570160-KM10', 'latitude': 37.7949086758744, 'longitude': -122.404037735679}, {'call_number': 2510051, 'unit_id': 'M28', 'incident_number': 75063, 'call_type': 'Medical Incident', 'call_date': '2000-09-07', 'watch_date': '2000-09-06', 'received_timestamp': '2000-09-07 06:45:27+00:00', 'entry_timestamp': '2000-09-07 06:46:31+00:00', 'dispatch_timestamp': '2000-09-07 06:47:13+00:00', 'response_timestamp': '2000-09-07 06:49:50+00:00', 'on_scene_timestamp': '2000-09-07 07:00:59+00:00', 'transport_timestamp': 'NaT', 'hospital_timestamp': 'NaT', 'call_final_disposition': 'Other', 'available_timestamp': '2000-09-07 07:25:42+00:00', 'address': '400 Block of FILBERT ST', 'city': 'SF', 'zipcode_of_incident': '94133', 'battalion': 'B01', 'station_area': '28', 'box': '0126', 'original_priority': '1', 'priority': '1', 'final_priority': 2, 'als_unit': True, 'call_typ